※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4393
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4393 LANG_CONSTINIT_WRITTEN
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4394 LANG_CONSTINIT_DEFINED_HERE

※ Nothing writes a `constinit` variable but its initializer.  By the time the
※ first constructor runs, the initializer has given it its value, and from
※ the startup function on its pages are read-only, a write there stopping the
※ program on a fault -- so it is refused here, where it is written, and the
※ note says which definition made it so.
※
※ Every way of writing is a write: assigning it, a field or an element of it,
※ handing it on as `&mut`, walking it with `&mut`, joining onto a list it is.
※ Reading it, and taking a `&` of it, are what the rest of the program does.

let std := ⎕import("std")

constinit let seed: u64 = ⎕auxv(6) ?? 7u64

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let read: &u64 = &seed
    seed ← read⌖ + 1u64
    0u6
